d for a child?J1J2bJ4.0aJ4.0bJ4.1 M6Sheet 5Doing it togetherWould your neighbour need this too? If yes, why would you each build it?J3bJ4.0bJ4.1 M7Sheet 6First move and the investment requiredWhat is realistic in twelve months with the people and money we have — and who owns it?J4.1  Technical track DraftTwo days, one cross-border immunization story. Day 1 covers the building blocks and gets everyone running on Heropa. Day 2 is teams building one part of the journey, then seeing it all work together. Draft for the team to confirm. Names and times are proposals. Day 1 · 30 November · Concepts and the OHS stack. By the end of the day you have captured data, synced it, run a workflow and started a dashboard, all on Heropa. T111:00–11:40Building with FHIR and the Open Health StackWhich FHIR resources, terminologies and tools carry this journey, and where does each lab use them?J1J3bJ4.0b T211:40–12:30Offline data captureHow does a form on a health worker's phone become a patient record, with no signal?J2aJ2b T313:30–13:50Trust between countries: SMART Trust and the GDHCNHow can a clinic in one country trust a vaccination record from another, and when is a card better than a link?J1J3aJ4.1 T413:50–15:00Workflows, sync and who sees whatWhat should happen next for this child, how does the record reach the server, and who is allowed to see it?J2bJ3bJ4.0bJ4.1 T515:30–16:30From records to chartsHow does a FHIR record become a row, a chart and a coverage number, and who accessed what?J2bJ3bJ4.1  Day 2 · 1 December · Teams build one app in the journey, show it, and then everything runs together. T611:00–11:30Verifying a card, sharing a linkHow does an app go from a scanned QR to a verified result, and from a shared link to the records behind it?J3aJ4.0bJ4.1 T711:30–16:15Team build, showcase and the journey togetherCan each team change one app in the journey and then run the whole journey live, from a birth abroad to a clinic back home to the family travelling again?J2bJ3aJ4.0aJ